WEBVTT

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:02.470
Section fifteen.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:04.430
Evaluation and evidence.

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.570
The purpose is to learn which stage succeeds,

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.750
which stage fails, and how far the measurements generalize.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.115
A single attractive score cannot answer all three

00:00:17.115 --> 00:00:17.555
questions.

00:00:27.047 --> 00:00:29.667
The frozen corpus has thirty repositories.

00:00:30.807 --> 00:00:32.167
Ten were development cases;

00:00:33.207 --> 00:00:37.087
twenty formed the evaluation partition, with eight public

00:00:37.087 --> 00:00:39.667
libraries and twelve synthetic cases.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.867
The registry has forty-two concepts,

00:00:43.527 --> 00:00:45.867
including four non-searchable Domains.

00:00:46.707 --> 00:00:50.027
Public labels were proposed and user-approved.

00:00:51.127 --> 00:00:55.107
Related initiatives were grouped, but policy clarification reused

00:00:55.107 --> 00:00:56.287
evaluation cases.

00:00:57.327 --> 00:00:59.247
The final round is regression validation,

00:01:00.047 --> 00:01:02.307
not untouched generalization evidence.

00:01:03.507 --> 00:01:05.747
Project-positive evidence is synthetic;

00:01:06.987 --> 00:01:09.567
private enterprise performance remains unestablished.

00:01:15.247 --> 00:01:19.227
Candidate recall asks whether expected IDs reached the shortlist.

00:01:20.107 --> 00:01:24.847
Both lexical methods covered all expected evaluation labels under

00:01:24.847 --> 00:01:25.787
generous caps.

00:01:27.348 --> 00:01:29.788
Classification then produced fifty true positives,

00:01:30.568 --> 00:01:32.948
zero false positives, and two misses:

00:01:33.988 --> 00:01:37.168
micro F one of ninety-eight percent.

00:01:37.168 --> 00:01:39.549
Both missing labels had been retrieved,

00:01:40.589 --> 00:01:43.949
locating those errors after candidate inclusion, without proving

00:01:43.949 --> 00:01:46.369
whether packing or model selection caused them.

00:01:51.847 --> 00:01:55.867
Taxonomy drafts passed structural checks and received qualitative

00:01:55.867 --> 00:01:59.567
acceptance, but no numeric human rubric was recorded.

00:02:00.747 --> 00:02:02.507
One repeated classification agreed;

00:02:03.187 --> 00:02:04.987
that is not long-run stability.

00:02:06.387 --> 00:02:06.807
Limited timing,

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:08.647
contract, race,

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:13.107
privacy, and recovery checks establish specific behaviors.

00:02:13.987 --> 00:02:17.827
They do not measure citation entailment or calibrated confidence.

00:02:18.607 --> 00:02:22.687
No complete RAGAS-style question-answering evaluation or

00:02:22.687 --> 00:02:25.427
independent production accuracy study was performed.

00:02:26.987 --> 00:02:29.767
Historical timings use nearest-rank percentiles from twenty

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:30.307
observations,

00:02:31.307 --> 00:02:32.467
not a production guarantee.

00:02:33.867 --> 00:02:36.827
Subscription-based Codex checks were supplementary, not

00:02:36.827 --> 00:02:39.227
replacements for real API validation.

00:02:44.387 --> 00:02:47.547
A stronger study needs independent annotations,

00:02:48.407 --> 00:02:52.647
unseen initiatives, harder neighbors, no-match cases, and broader

00:02:52.647 --> 00:02:53.187
languages.

00:02:54.487 --> 00:02:57.367
Freeze policy and source snapshots before comparing methods.

00:02:58.607 --> 00:03:02.167
Group related repositories when splitting, and report per-kind

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:02.647
errors,

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:03.587
abstention,

00:03:04.327 --> 00:03:04.807
source support,

00:03:05.607 --> 00:03:07.627
correction effort, and total cost.

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:11.347
Confidence intervals and model-winner claims should follow

00:03:11.347 --> 00:03:15.587
adequate data rather than being manufactured from this small

00:03:15.587 --> 00:03:16.447
reused set.
